{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_018gvW91ZeCwfSSFGUdbLaSB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** go-unix-utils is a specification-driven pipeline that re-implements classic Unix utilities in Go, verifying them against GNU reference binaries through differential testing. The goal is to stress-test the mage-claude-orchestrator code generation system.\n\n**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). `cmd/` holds per-utility Go implementations, `pkg/testutils/` provides the differential testing harness, `pkg/sys/` wraps platform syscalls, `pkg/format/` provides shared formatting. Specs in `docs/` are human-authored; code generation targets only `cmd/` and `pkg/`.\n\n**Current state (from source code):** All foundational packages exist (`pkg/testutils`, `pkg/sys`, `pkg/format`). Utilities with complete code: `cmd/cat`, `cmd/du`, `cmd/ls`, `cmd/sponge`, `cmd/wc`, `cmd/version`.\n\n**Priorities:** Releases 00.0, 01.1, 01.2, 01.3, 03.0, 04.0 all have code on the branch. Releases 02.0, 02.1, 02.2 have pending specs (human-authored, not actionable by the pipeline). Release 04.1 (ls-extended) has specs complete but requires PRD content not in context. The highest-value actionable work is filling test coverage gaps in existing utilities — `cmd/cat` has the largest gap, with 4 untested PRD requirements (R3.2, R4.1, R4.2, R4.4) covering cross-boundary squeeze behavior and non-printing character display.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"prd006-cat R3.2, R4.1, R4.2, R4.4: Differential tests for cross-boundary squeeze and non-printing display\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - cmd/cat/cat_test.go (existing differential test patterns, helpers, TestMain setup)\n      - cmd/cat/main.go (implementation of squeeze state R3.2, non-printing display R4.1, tab exemption R4.2, show tabs R4.4)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd006-cat.yaml (requirement definitions for R3.2, R4.1, R4.2, R4.4)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (RunDiffTests API, DiffTest struct fields)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/cat/cat_test.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add differential tests for cross-boundary squeeze and non-printing character display\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Add TestCatCrossBoundarySqueeze testing prd006-cat R3.2: when -s is active, squeeze state (prevBlank) persists across file boundaries. Create two files where the first ends with consecutive blank lines and the second starts with blank lines, then verify -s produces a single blank line at the boundary.\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Add TestCatNonPrintingControl testing prd006-cat R4.1 for control characters: with -v flag, bytes 0x01-0x1F (excluding 0x09 tab and 0x0A newline) are displayed as ^A through ^_ caret notation, and byte 0x7F is displayed as ^?.\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Add TestCatNonPrintingHighByte testing prd006-cat R4.1 for high bytes: with -v flag, bytes in the range 0x80-0xFF are displayed with M- prefix notation. Control-range high bytes (0x80-0x9F) become M-^@ through M-^_, printable-range high bytes (0xA0-0xFE) become M- followed by the character, and 0xFF becomes M-^?.\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Add TestCatTabExemptFromV testing prd006-cat R4.2: when only -v is given without -T, tab characters (0x09) pass through unchanged in the output.\"\n      - id: R5\n        text: \"Add TestCatShowTabs testing prd006-cat R4.4: when -T is active, tab characters are displayed as ^I. Test both -T alone and -T combined with -v to verify the interaction.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Follow the existing differential test pattern: each test function creates fixture files with writeTestFile, then calls testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBinary, refBinary, tests) comparing Go cat against gcat.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Each test function calls t.Parallel() and uses t.TempDir() for file isolation, matching existing tests like TestCatFileRead and TestCatSqueeze.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Non-printing character test files use string literals with Go escape sequences (\\\\x01, \\\\x7f, \\\\x80, \\\\xff) to inject specific byte values into fixture files via writeTestFile.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"TestCatCrossBoundarySqueeze passes: runs at least two DiffTest cases verifying -s squeeze across file boundaries, comparing Go cat output byte-for-byte against gcat.\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"TestCatNonPrintingControl passes: runs DiffTest cases with -v flag on files containing control bytes (0x01, 0x1F, 0x7F), verifying ^X caret notation matches gcat.\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"TestCatNonPrintingHighByte passes: runs DiffTest cases with -v flag on files containing high bytes (0x80, 0x9F, 0xC0, 0xFF), verifying M- prefix notation matches gcat.\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"TestCatTabExemptFromV passes: runs DiffTest cases confirming -v alone preserves tab characters in output, matching gcat.\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"TestCatShowTabs passes: runs DiffTest cases confirming -T transforms tabs to ^I both standalone and combined with -v, matching gcat.\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/cat/... passes with zero failures including all pre-existing tests.\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":85799,"cache_read_input_tokens":19289,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":85799},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b2469e57-f99d-4f52-8547-77e7dab06d24","uuid":"f93c715b-8dcc-4118-988f-d49370f918c5"}
